WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.205
Never used an AI chat tool?
This section is for you.

00:00:04.205 --> 00:00:08.382
You'll learn what these tools are,
how to get started with Gemini,

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:11.650
and four habits for
using any AI tool safely.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.268
An AI assistant is a chat tool.

00:00:14.268 --> 00:00:18.116
You type a request in everyday words,
and it writes a reply.

00:00:18.116 --> 00:00:20.450
It works by predicting likely words,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.130
which is why it can sound sure,
and still be wrong.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.497
Several assistants have free versions:
Gemini from Google,

00:00:28.497 --> 00:00:32.774
ChatGPT from OpenAI, Microsoft Copilot,
and Claude from Anthropic.

00:00:32.774 --> 00:00:36.285
There are also research tools
that show their sources,

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:39.988
and notebook tools that answer
from documents you upload.

00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:43.580
The basic skills carry
over from one to the next.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.778
We'll practice with Gemini. It has
a free version, runs in a web browser,

00:00:48.778 --> 00:00:51.325
and works with a regular Google account.

00:00:51.325 --> 00:00:53.624
Go to gemini.google.com and sign in.

00:00:53.624 --> 00:00:58.843
The reading walks you through every step,
including age rules and privacy settings.

00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:02.660
You don't need to pay,
or sign up for a student offer.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.739
Habit one: ask clearly.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.298
Say what you want, give the background,
and describe the answer you need.

00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:13.303
Compare "Tell me about rural
hospitals" with "In five sentences,

00:01:13.303 --> 00:01:18.570
explain what a critical access hospital
is, for a first-year college student."

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:23.469
Habit two: check the answer.
If the reply lists sources, open them.

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:27.388
Confirm key facts, numbers,
and names with a trusted website,

00:01:27.388 --> 00:01:29.980
such as a government or university page.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.110
If you can't find a source,
treat the claim as unverified.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.613
Habit three: protect privacy.

00:01:36.613 --> 00:01:41.181
Never paste real patient information,
passwords, or confidential files.

00:01:41.181 --> 00:01:45.179
On a personal account,
some chats are read by human reviewers.

00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:47.145
In Gemini's activity settings,

00:01:47.145 --> 00:01:52.050
you can stop saving new chats to
your activity, and delete past chats.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.827
Habit four: test before you trust.

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:59.368
Before relying on a tool for a task,
try it on a few realistic examples,

00:01:59.368 --> 00:02:03.536
including messy ones, and compare
its answers with the right ones.

00:02:03.536 --> 00:02:06.860
That's scenario testing,
in its simplest form.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.168
In the reading,
you'll practice all four habits

00:02:10.168 --> 00:02:12.989
with short tasks set in
a fictional rural clinic.

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:15.866
If you can't, or don't want to,
create an account,

00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:19.820
you can follow along with
the examples in the reading instead.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:25.324
Ask clearly, check the answer, protect
privacy, and test before you trust.

00:02:25.324 --> 00:02:28.332
AI can save you time,
but you stay in charge.

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:33.440
That wraps up the videos for Tutorial 5.
Now, on to the practice tasks.
